import json,xml.etree.ElementTree as E
from pathlib import Path
ns={'a':'http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom'}
lines=['# E0007 literature and status search — 2026-10-12','', 'No exact published solution verified. This bounded search is not evidence that no solution exists.','', '## Source confirmed','', 'Rick Durrett, Coexistence in stochastic spatial models, The Annals of Applied Probability 19(2) (2009), 477–496. DOI: 10.1214/08-AAP590. arXiv:0906.2293v1. Problem 1, PDF p. 3 (downloaded source.pdf, extracted source.txt). The initial 09-PS139 DOI lookup was erroneous; later lookups used the confirmed DOI.','', '> Problem 1. Show that species 1 outcompetes species 2 holds if the dispersal distributions are the same and β1/δ1 > β2/δ2. The simulation in Figure 2 gives some support for this conjecture.','', 'The model is defined on Z^2 on PDF pp. 1–2. Birth rates are total individual rates with offspring displacement probabilities p_i(y), and only vacant destinations accept births. Preceding Theorem 1, PDF p. 2, defines exclusion as P(ξ_t(x)=2)→0 for translation-invariant initial law with P(ξ_0(x)=1)>0. No irreducibility, symmetry, range, or initial ergodicity hypothesis is explicit in Problem 1. The literal initial-law mixture issue is explained in ATTEMPT.md.','', '## All online requests','', 'The URLs below preserve every query, service, date, HTTP outcome and response filename. Rate-limited requests are failures, not negative search results. The OpenAlex source lookup succeeded with work ID W2057281188; citing-work requests were made but rate limited. Semantic Scholar citing-source request succeeded, returning 27 records. GitHub returned one repository; it is not a mathematical proof.','']
for line in Path('search_log.jsonl').read_text(encoding='utf8').splitlines():
 a=json.loads(line);lines.append('- '+a.get('date','2026-10-12')+' — '+a['url']+' — '+str(a.get('status',a.get('error')))+' — '+a.get('file',''))
lines+=['','## Candidate references and disposition','', 'Joseph P. Stover, A stochastic comparison result for the multitype contact process with unequal death rates, Statistics & Probability Letters 162 (2020), 108763. DOI 10.1016/j.spl.2020.108763; arXiv:1908.06628v2 (17 May 2021). Full text downloaded as comparison.pdf and comparison.txt. Proposition 2.1, PDF pp. 4–5, concerns coordinatewise favorable birth and death rates. Theorem 2.2, PDF p. 5, gives a sufficient inequality involving λ(β,c,α)>λ_c for strong survival from one particle against an all-opponent background. It does not assert type-opponent density tends to zero and does not cover all ratio-ordered parameters. Theorem 2.2 is therefore a lead, not SOLVED_IN_LITERATURE. Per-neighbor birth rates in this paper must be multiplied by 2d to match Durrett\'s total-rate convention. Its introduction explicitly labels the birth/death ratio assertion a conjecture.','', 'Thomas Mountford, Pedro Luis Barrios Pantoja, Daniel Valesin, The asymmetric multitype contact process, Stochastic Processes and their Applications 129(8) (2019), 2783–2822. DOI 10.1016/j.spa.2018.08.006; arXiv:1803.01533v1. Downloaded asymmetric.pdf/txt. Theorems 1.1 and 1.2, PDF pp. 2–3, prove survival/takeover and complete convergence under birth-rate ordering; the generator and introduction on PDF p. 1 explicitly set BOTH death rates to 1. Thus these are equal-death special cases, not an answer to unequal-death ratio ordering. It clarifies the initial-state quantifier: convergence from arbitrary states includes a component with only type 2 when type 1 becomes extinct.','', 'Isabella Alvarenga and Daniel Valesin, Interface for variants of the contact process, arXiv:2602.23149v1 (26 February 2026). Downloaded interface.pdf/txt. Theorems 4 and 5, PDF p. 4, concern one-dimensional Heaviside initial states and interface tightness/CLT. The same page explicitly says every occupied site dies at rate 1. Different initial states/dimension and equal death rates; not a solution.','', 'Marcelo Martins de Oliveira and Ronald Dickman, The advantage of being slow: the quasi-neutral contact process, Physical Review E 96 (2017), 032113; arXiv:1705.03819v2. Abstract checked via arXiv API (slow.xml). It concerns equal birth/death ratios, extinction advantage in finite spatial systems, and environmental variation. No full-text theorem verified; numerical/finite-size lead, not a counterexample to infinite-volume strict ratio ordering.','', 'J. Theodore Cox, Richard Durrett and Edwin A. Perkins, Voter model perturbations and reaction diffusion equations, Astérisque 349 (2013); arXiv:1103.1676v1. Abstract checked through voter.xml; focuses on two-state voter perturbations in d≥3 (Lotka–Volterra/cooperation/nonlinear voter examples), not the entire three-state competing contact-process parameter space on Z^2. A potential technique, not an exact-match theorem.','', 'Claudia Neuhauser, Ergodic theorems for the multitype contact process, Probability Theory and Related Fields 91 (1992), 467–506. DOI 10.1007/BF01192067. Metadata verified with Crossref; equal-death theorem quoted by the original source and discussed in the two full-text later papers. Not an unequal-death solution.','', 'Other returned arXiv entries include contact processes with seasons, frozen/sterile states, mutating species, symbiosis, density-dependent births, allelopathy, and tree coexistence. Those change the model or parameter hypotheses. Their exact titles/authors/IDs are retained below to keep search results auditable.','']
seen=set()
for file in ['arxiv.xml','arxiv_target.xml','slow.xml','voter.xml']:
 for e in E.parse(file).findall('a:entry',ns):
  aid=e.findtext('a:id',namespaces=ns)
  if aid in seen:continue
  seen.add(aid);title=' '.join(e.findtext('a:title',namespaces=ns).split());authors=', '.join(a.findtext('a:name',namespaces=ns) for a in e.findall('a:author',ns));date=e.findtext('a:published',namespaces=ns)
  lines.append('- '+authors+'. '+title+'. '+aid+'; '+date+'.')
lines+=['','## Read-only local/brain searches','', 'Called brain.py recall with "two-type contact process unequal death rates" and "contact process mistakes", and math_recall.py with "multitype contact process Neuhauser Durrett competitive exclusion". Results were largely irrelevant and are not mathematical evidence. The brain command reported an automatic cache-refresh attempt that failed; no brain write command was invoked.','', 'Initial rg invocation on the literal Windows wildcard failed (rg does not expand it). Corrected with Path.glob over probability_1000_intake_* and a read-only search of .jsonl/.md/.json files in those directories and codex_pool_2026_10_10. No E0007 hits; saved prior_hits.txt. Read git ls-tree origin/master and filtered paths for E0007/unequal-death; no matching paths, saved repo_paths.txt. No working-tree changes or commits.','', 'Search coverage is bounded: API result limits, missing newly indexed papers, rate limits, and title/keyword mismatches remain possible. No verdict SOLVED_IN_LITERATURE is claimed.']
Path('LITERATURE.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
# Print metadata needed to check exact bibliography.
for file in ['crossref.json','crossref_target.json']:
 for w in json.loads(Path(file).read_text())['message']['items']:
  if w.get('DOI') in ['10.1016/j.spa.2018.08.006','10.1016/j.spl.2020.108763']:print(w.get('title'),w.get('author'),w.get('volume'),w.get('issue'),w.get('page'),w.get('article-number'))
